## Overview

This repository contains web development exercises and projects created as part of Coursera learning assignments. The files cover different foundational frontend topics, including webpage structure, styling, form validation, and a solar system page.

The repository is intended as a learning portfolio showing practice with HTML and CSS. Refer to each source file to explore its specific implementation.

## Projects and Files

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| `index.html` | Main HTML practice page; inspect the file for its specific content. |
| `mywebpage.html` | A separate webpage exercise. |
| `form_validation.html` | HTML page related to form validation. |
| `form_validation.txt` | Supporting text or assignment material related to form validation. |
| `solarsystem.html` | A webpage about the solar system. |
| `style.css` | CSS styles used by one or more pages. |
| `AssignmentCoursera/` | Directory shown in the repository listing; explore it for additional assignment files. |

## Technology Stack

- **HTML5** — structures webpages and content.
- **CSS3** — styles page elements and layout.

## Getting Started

No build tools or backend services are required for the listed static HTML and CSS files.

1. Clone the repository:

   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/RabadeJanhvi-45/Coursera-Web-Development-Projectst.git
   ```

2. Open the repository folder in VS Code or another editor.
3. Open any `.html` file in a browser to view the page.
4. To edit the project, modify the HTML or CSS and refresh the browser to see the changes.

For a convenient development workflow, you can use the Live Server extension in VS Code.

## What This Repository Demonstrates

- Creating webpages with HTML.
- Applying CSS styling to web content.
- Practicing form-related markup and validation concepts.
- Organizing multiple learning exercises in one repository.
- Iterating on frontend work through source-code changes.

